MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The penetrant fits the practical repair work suggested by my hose clamps: loosening stuck hardware is a plausible need alongside fastening and adjusting parts.",
    "The heavy-duty VELCRO tape connects naturally to my duct tape and vinyl cement purchases, while rubber grommets complement my wire connectors by protecting wires at pass-through holes. Both offer useful ways to secure or protect things."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The precision depth gauge, polishing compounds, and IC test leads require specific tasks that my repair supplies do not establish. Owning repair materials does not mean I currently measure precision depths, polish metal, or test integrated circuits.",
    "The check valve, battery lugs, and single-size nut pack depend on matching fittings, cable gauges, or bolt sizes. I have no matching project in mind, and a hundred identical nuts would be excessive without one."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My clamp purchases seemed to be treated as a reason to recommend almost any mechanical hardware, even when its purpose and dimensions are unrelated to what I have used.",
    "My electrical connector purchase seemed to imply interest in both circuit testing and heavy battery wiring, although those involve different jobs from connecting smaller wires."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Several of my purchases are versatile fastening, adhesive, or repair supplies. Recommendations feel more useful when they support those practical functions without requiring an unmentioned specialized project.",
    "Compatibility and quantity matter to my willingness to choose something now. An assortment can offer flexibility, but it still needs a relevant use; a specialized fitting or large pack needs a much clearer match."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my practical repair interests, but often stretched them into specialized tasks and hardware needs that my purchases do not establish."
}
